{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Vite + React + Vitest — good, that's locked as the stack. Before I can shape the foundation mission, I need to know what this app actually *is*: what do you want to build here, in one or two plain-language sentences? (I only need enough to pick the one thin vertical slice that proves the skeleton and the tests are really wired together — I won't design the features.)","recommended":"Tell me the product in your own words — e.g. \"a dashboard for tracking X\", \"a tool that lets me do Y\" — and I'll turn it into a bootable skeleton with one honest end-to-end slice."},"prd":"# Mission: Establish foundation — Vite + React + Vitest skeleton\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up a bootable Vite + React skeleton with a working Vitest test system, proven connected by one thin vertical slice.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- The project boots and renders something in the browser.\n- Vitest runs from a single command and a human can watch it pass.\n- One thin vertical slice exercises the skeleton and is covered by a test.\n**Out of Scope:**\n- (to be captured) product features named during Align are deferred to the vision doc.\n**Constraints:**\n- Stack: Vite + React + Vitest (captain-confirmed).\n"}

